                <pb facs="0408" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.E/180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cottrell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-17T10:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                                1923—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Bolivian Government announces it will not concur [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >sic</hi>] in Pan American Conference because of Chile’s unwillingness to
                    accept a revision of the treaty of 1904.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
